`writeFile` will throw `ENOENT` if the parent directory of `outputPath` does not exist. For example, `storybook ai prepare -o some/new/dir/prompt.md` fails if `some/new/dir/` hasn't been created yet. Consider adding a `mkdir` call before writing:
```ts
import { mkdir, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';
import { dirname, resolve } from 'node:path';

const outputPath = resolve(output);
await mkdir(dirname(outputPath), { recursive: true });
await writeFile(outputPath, markdownOutput, 'utf-8');
```
Otherwise the error message from `handleCommandFailure` will be confusing to users who don't realize they need to pre-create the directory.
